  "chapter": {
    "number": 31,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(32) A Psalm of",
          {
            "noteId": 55
          },
          "instruction by David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed are they whose transgressions are forgiven, and who sins are covered.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the man to whom the Lord will not impute sin, and whose mouth there is no guile.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because I kept silence, my bones waxed old, from my crying all the day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For day and night your hand was heavy upon me: I became thoroughly miserable while a",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 56
          },
          {
            "text": "thorn was fastened in me. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I acknowledged my sin, and hid not my iniquity: I said, I will confess my iniquity to the Lord against myself; and you forgave the ungodliness of my heart. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore shall every holy one pray to you in a fit time: only in the deluge of many waters they shall not come near to him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You are my refuge from the affliction that encompasses me; my joy, to deliver me from them that have compassed me. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will instruct you and guide you in this way wherein you shall go: I will fix my eyes upon you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be you⌃ not as horse and mule, which have no understanding;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 57
          },
          {
            "text": "but you must constrain their jaws with bit and curb, lest they should come near to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Many are the scourges of the sinner: but him that hopes in the Lord mercy shall compass about.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be glad in the Lord, and exult, you⌃ righteous: and glory, all you⌃ that are upright in heart.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
